course: dictionary
lesson: 10454
title: Trustworthy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Trustworthy means you can trust a person or thing. A trustworthy person is honest and reliable: you can believe what they say, and you can depend on them to do what they promise. Look at the parts of the word: trust, and worthy, which means deserving. So a trustworthy person is someone who deserves to be trusted.
explain: «A trustworthy person keeps a secret.» The clue is keeps a secret. Someone who keeps your secret safe is someone you can rely on, so trustworthy must mean reliable and honest. Being trusted to keep something safe is an honour.
explain: A thing can be trustworthy too. A trustworthy website or source of information is one that is likely to be true. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word, such as "can be trusted", and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Trustworthy means honest and reliable: you can believe what someone says and depend on them.
fact: A trustworthy source of information is one that is likely to be true.
fact: Useful phrases: a trustworthy friend, a trustworthy adult, a trustworthy website.
fact: Trustworthiness is the noun: it is the quality of being trustworthy.
fact: «Being good when no one is watching is what makes you trustworthy.»
exercise: «A trustworthy person keeps a secret.» What does trustworthy mean here? | Always late for school | Very tall and strong | *Honest and reliable, someone you can depend on | Loud and bossy
exercise: In safety lessons, which is a trustworthy adult to ask for help? | A person who shouts at you in the park | Someone who tells you to keep secrets from your parents | *A teacher or a police officer | A stranger who offers you sweets
exercise: Which word is the noun for being trustworthy? | Distrust | Trusting | Untrustworthy | *Trustworthiness
test: Which website is most likely to be trustworthy for facts about volcanoes? | A video with a rude joke in the title | *A site written by a university or science museum | A site with no author and no sources | A pop-up saying you have won a prize
test: Mia's friend tells her a secret and asks her to keep it safe. What does a trustworthy friend do? | Tells the whole class at lunch | *Keeps the secret safe | Forgets about it and laughs at her friend | Posts the secret online for fun
exam: «Ravi returns the book he borrowed, on time, and never breaks a promise.» What does this show about Ravi? | He is a bad reader | He is always lost | He is unhappy | *He is trustworthy
